## Summary

The bug was in `resolveOption(String opt)` in `CommandLine.java`. It called `Util.stripLeadingHyphens(opt)`, which correctly returns `null` when given a `null` option name, but the method then unconditionally did `opt.equals(...)` inside the lookup loop, throwing an NPE on a null `opt`.

Fix (in `src/main/java/org/apache/commons/cli/CommandLine.java`):

```java
private Option resolveOption(String opt) {
    opt = Util.stripLeadingHyphens(opt);
    if (opt == null) {
        return null;
    }
    for (final Option option : options) {
        if (opt.equals(option.getOpt()) || opt.equals(option.getLongOpt())) {
            return option;
        }
    }
    return null;
}
```

Now a `null` option name resolves to "no option" (`null`), which flows through `getOptionValue` correctly returning the supplied default or `null`. Ran the full Maven test suite (`mvn test`) — all tests pass, no failures.

